SUMMARY:NATUREFEST
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a FREE\, family-friendly celebration of nature in North Carolina! Explore the wonders of nature—from plant powers to live animals to fairy house building—through fun\, hands-on stations setup throughout the Garden. Designed for families with children up to age 10\, this outdoor event is a great way to connect with nature and enjoy a day of learning and discovery together. Locopops available for purchase! \nWe’ll be joined by community partners Chapel Hill Public Library\, New Hope Bird Alliance\, NC Herpetological Society\, NC Science Trail\, and Triangle Land Conservancy. \nNo registration required.
URL:https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/naturefest/
LOCATION:North Carolina Botanical Garden\, 100 Old Mason Farm Road\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27517\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncbg.unc.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/963/2026/07/20241019-NatureFest-151-scaled.jpg
