SUMMARY:Lunchbox Talk: Great Wildlife Migrations
DESCRIPTION:with Clyde Sorenson\, Alumni Associate Distinguished Undergraduate Professor\, NC State University \nJoin Clyde Sorenson for a look at one of the most spectacular animal behaviors on Earth: migration. Why do animals migrate\, and what are the risks and rewards of making these incredible journeys? Clyde will explore several important migrations in North America\, including those of monarch butterflies\, humpback whales\, neotropical migrant songbirds\, and waterfowl\, and discuss the conservation challenges these animals face.\n\nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/lunchbox-talk-great-wildlife-migrations/
LOCATION:North Carolina Botanical Garden\, 100 Old Mason Farm Road\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27517\, United States
CATEGORIES:Learn,Lunchbox Talks
GEO:35.901081;-79.031939
