SUMMARY:Nature Tales: Going Batty (AM session)
DESCRIPTION:Ages: 3-7 with participating adult\nFee: $5 per child (No fee for Members and families receiving SNAP benefits) \nGet batty with us for a fun storytime all about these fascinating nighttime flyers! After stories\, we’ll head into the Garden to look for the places bats might roost\, the insects they love to eat\, and clues that bats are part of our Garden ecosystem. \nThis program takes place in our beautiful new Wilkinson Outdoor Classroom! \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/nature-tales-going-batty-am-session/
LOCATION:North Carolina Botanical Garden\, 100 Old Mason Farm Road\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27517\, United States
CATEGORIES:Learn
